      "kind": "unsafe",
      "source_path": ".Jules/sentinel.md",
      "line": 17,
      "text": "**Vulnerability:** The use of `sql.unsafe()` to perform dynamic string interpolation for the `ORDER BY` clause was identified as an anti-pattern. While the specific logic was protected by an `if/else` block, `sql.unsafe()` should be avoided"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unsafe",
      "source_path": ".Jules/sentinel.md",
      "line": 18,
      "text": "**Learning:** Removing `sql.unsafe()` by directly duplicating queries creates highly unmaintainable code that violates DRY principles."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unsafe",
      "source_path": ".Jules/sentinel.md",
      "line": 19,
      "text": "**Prevention:** Rather than using dynamic SQL via `sql.unsafe()` or duplicating queries entirely, conditionally sort parameterized dynamic logic by embedding standard SQL `CASE WHEN ... THEN ... END` structures directly into the `ORDER BY` "
    },
    {
      "kind": "unsafe",
      "source_path": ".Jules/sentinel.md",
      "line": 21,
      "text": "## 2026-03-31 - [SQL Injection Risk via sql.unsafe()]"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unsafe",
      "source_path": ".Jules/sentinel.md",
      "line": 22,
      "text": "**Vulnerability:** The `app/api/v1/terms/route.ts` endpoint used `sql.unsafe(orderBy)` to dynamically insert an ORDER BY clause. While the input was constrained via an if/else block, using `unsafe()` with string interpolation sets a dangero"
    },
    {
      "kind": "unsafe",
      "source_path": ".Jules/sentinel.md",
      "line": 23,
      "text": "**Learning:** The Neon serverless database utility does not support safe dynamic column or keyword insertion via `sql.unsafe()`. This forces us to either use unsafe string manipulation or separate queries."
    },
    {
      "kind": "unsafe",
      "source_path": ".Jules/sentinel.md",
      "line": 24,
      "text": "**Prevention:** Avoid `sql.unsafe()` entirely for dynamic queries. Instead, write separate, full SQL queries for different sorting/filtering scenarios, or use a query builder that safely handles dynamic identifiers."
    },
